1
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:20,810
Hello.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,850
Is this Officer Song?

3
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,420
I'm Yang Jintian's sister.

4
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,420
[TAXI]

5
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:35,450
Kids these days are hotheaded.

6
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,330
One little disagreement,

7
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,980
and they're fighting with a cab driver.

8
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:39,220
You're responsible for him.

9
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,580
You ought to teach him how to behave.

10
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:42,500
Wake up.

11
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:45,770
Look how drunk he is.

12
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:52,540
Did you hit someone?

13
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:55,050
I got hit.

14
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,010
Where are you hurt?

15
00:00:57,030 --> 00:00:57,770
Is it bad?

16
00:00:58,350 --> 00:00:59,180
He isn't hurt.

17
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:00,980
His arm's a bit red from being grabbed.

18
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,580
He's fine.

19
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,480
Officer,

20
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:07,840
where's the man who hit him?

21
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,930
First, let's get one thing straight.

22
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:10,850
This wasn't an assault.

23
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:12,210
They were drunk and started it.

24
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:14,740
You. Tell us

25
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:15,940
how you ended up

26
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:17,180
picking a fight with a woman in her eighties.

27
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,410
They were the ones who got hit.

28
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:19,850
Where's the man who hit them?

29
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:21,410
What's with the attitude?

30
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,570
Self-reflection comes first. Got it?

31
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:24,930
Is this the example you set for him?

32
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,820
They had too much to drink

33
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,410
and hailed a cab to get home.

34
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:33,130
An elderly woman nearby wanted a cab too.

35
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,100
The driver felt sorry for her

36
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,380
and wanted to take her instead.

37
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,380
But these kids

38
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:39,690
wouldn't let him.

39
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,380
Then an argument started.

40
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,290
Officer,

41
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:43,900
I know my brother.

42
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,570
He might not give someone else his seat,

43
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,690
but he'd never throw the first punch.

44
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:53,410
Are you really going to keep making a fuss over this?

45
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,460
Fighting over a seat with a woman in her eighties.

46
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:57,490
What kind of person does that?

47
00:01:58,230 --> 00:01:59,900
Scum, that's who.

48
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,290
Who are you calling scum?

49
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:02,930
Sit down.

50
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,050
- Who are you calling scum? - Sit down!

51
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:04,900
- Who's scum? - Sit down!

52
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:05,700
Who's scum?

53
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:06,490
What are you doing?

54
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,170
Sit down. I'll handle this.

55
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,450
The man who hit them is in there, right?

56
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,340
I saw your cab parked outside.

57
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,260
Ma'am,

58
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,350
what exactly are you trying to do?

59
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,100
Didn't I tell you?

60
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:35,410
Both sides are at fault.

61
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:36,660
They were drunk and started it.

62
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:38,130
Then ask him to come out

63
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:39,290
so we can talk this through.

64
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,450
It was just a little scuffle.

65
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:42,170
Settle it privately.

66
00:02:42,190 --> 00:02:43,730
I don't understand why you keep protecting

67
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:44,540
this driver.

68
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:46,100
If he won't even show his face,

69
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,570
what's left to talk about?

70
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,100
Tell you what.

71
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,130
Do you want compensation?

72
00:02:52,150 --> 00:02:53,820
I can run that by the driver.

73
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:55,450
No.

74
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:57,340
An apology will do.

75
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,940
To my brother, in person.

76
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,850
The driver's being very cooperative.

77
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:20,890
He's willing to pay.

78
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,130
Just tell me how much.

79
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,220
[Public Security Mediation Agreement]

80
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,460
[Parties Involved: Chen Mingsheng]

81
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:30,730
He's willing to pay,

82
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,980
but he won't even come out and talk?

83
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,780
[Yang Zhao]

84
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:40,660
Mingsheng,

85
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:42,660
she signed the settlement agreement.

86
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,170
I've never met a woman this stubborn.

87
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:48,050
Mingsheng, I don't get it.

88
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,890
Why did you offer her money in the first place?

89
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,410
All right, give it a rest.

90
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,230
She didn't even ask for his number.

91
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:55,340
I don't think she was after money.

92
00:03:58,030 --> 00:03:59,130
I'll pay.

93
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:01,450
But don't give her my number.

94
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:02,980
Right.

95
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,010
We can't give her your number.

96
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:04,980
Less trouble that way.

97
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:23,740
[Public Security Mediation Agreement]

98
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:30,140
[Parties Involved: Chen Mingsheng, Yang Zhao]

99
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,860
[Parties Involved: Chen Mingsheng]

100
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:55,900
[Jiang Ming]

101
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,700
[Jiang Ming; Parties Involved: Chen Mingsheng]

102
00:05:06,830 --> 00:05:07,580
Jiang Ming.

103
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,170
Jiang, J-I-A-N-G.

104
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:09,860
Ming, M-I-N-G.

105
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:11,900
Yang Zhao.

106
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:14,500
I'm Yang Zhao, an artifact conservator.

107
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,700
[Public Security]

108
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:27,100
Ms. Yang?

109
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:28,660
Anything you need?

110
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:30,330
Could I see the driver?

111
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:33,540
Ms. Yang, what are you trying to do?

112
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:34,940
I want to know

113
00:05:35,590 --> 00:05:36,980
why he won't meet with me.

114
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,420
The mediation is over.

115
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:41,570
You've already signed the settlement agreement.

116
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:42,690
If you have something to say,

117
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:44,060
I can pass it on to him.

118
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:44,690
Okay?

119
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,130
Can I see him?

120
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:49,020
The driver said

121
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,290
he could pay a reasonable amount,

122
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:51,290
but there was no need to meet.

123
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:52,410
Less trouble for everyone that way.

124
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,610
That's what he said?

125
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:54,410
Yeah.

126
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,340
Wait.

127
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,370
His name's Chen Mingsheng, right?

128
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:05,050
Then tell him to pay.

129
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:06,410
Have him bring 5,000 yuan to this address.

130
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,250
I'll be waiting.

131
00:06:07,270 --> 00:06:08,140
Five thousand?

132
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:10,340
I haven't...

133
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,410
[Lingkong Police Station]
I haven't agreed to that.

134
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:12,540
Ma'am!

135
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,540
Excuse me, can I ask you something?

136
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,140
Which cab company

137
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:19,370
uses cars like yours?

138
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,580
Lots of companies use this model.

139
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,900
You'd have to go by the plate number.

140
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:25,220
All our plates start with C.

141
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:27,780
If it starts with J,

142
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,460
which company does it belong to?

143
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:35,850
We don't have a cab like that.

144
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:37,730
Thanks.

145
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:39,700
The plate prefix is right,

146
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,020
but we don't have that particular cab.

147
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,580
It's almost shift change.

148
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,980
All our cabs will be coming back.

149
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,050
If it's urgent, you can wait over there and see.

150
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:49,410
Okay, thanks.

151
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:49,850
No problem.

152
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:38,620
[TAXI]

153
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:46,220
Huaken Gold Tower, please.

154
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:51,370
Sorry,

155
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,580
I'm soaking wet.

156
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:54,290
I'll give you a little extra when we arrive.

157
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,020
What happened?

158
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:22,900
[TAXI]

159
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,380
Sorry, the cab broke down.

160
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,010
You'll have to get out and call another cab.

161
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,580
[Name: Chen Mingsheng]

162
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,100
Chen Mingsheng?

163
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:56,940
That was you at the station yesterday, right?

164
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,700
I'm Yang Zhao.

165
00:09:02,730 --> 00:09:03,410
I know.

166
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,820
You knew it was me

167
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,130
before I even got in, didn't you?

168
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:12,370
No.

169
00:09:13,790 --> 00:09:14,340
It was a coincidence.

170
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:20,700
It's pouring.

171
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,650
The car's going to flood at this rate.

172
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:23,980
Let's get out and try pushing it.

173
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:25,580
No need.

174
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:28,420
We're close to Huaken Gold Tower.

175
00:09:29,550 --> 00:09:30,530
Just walk from here.

176
00:09:30,550 --> 00:09:31,820
I can help you push.

177
00:09:32,150 --> 00:09:32,940
I can manage.

178
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:40,490
Why have you been avoiding me, Jiang Ming?

179
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,850
Do you really not want to see me?

180
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:46,580
I don't.

181
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:56,100
[Public Security Mediation Agreement]

182
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,100
♪I remember how my fingertips♪

183
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:26,100
♪Once lingered on your face♪

184
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,180
Elephant up.

185
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,500
♪Yet my memories of you...♪

186
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,980
Check.

187
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:35,610
You're back.

188
00:10:36,150 --> 00:10:37,010
Out driving all night again?

189
00:10:37,010 --> 00:10:38,500
♪We parted without a word in the end♪

190
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:42,580
♪Silently, we drifted apart♪

191
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,140
♪I don't blame you♪

192
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:45,740
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

193
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:49,220
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

194
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:53,460
♪I wanted us to share♪

195
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,740
♪A simple life without regrets♪

196
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,220
♪And I almost told you♪

197
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,540
♪What that rush of tears♪

198
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:03,940
♪Had moved me to promise♪

199
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:06,620
♪It's a shame that you and I♪

200
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:08,260
♪Were bound to face a rough road♪

201
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,740
♪Bound to go nowhere♪

202
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,540
♪I won't be sad♪

203
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:15,700
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

204
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:19,460
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

205
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:22,820
♪I won't cry♪

206
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:37,660
♪I won't cry♪

207
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:35,580
Yang Zhao,

208
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:38,820
could you

209
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:44,820
give me a few days?

210
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:48,580
When I come back,

211
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:53,650
I'll tell you everything.

212
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:58,090
Okay.

213
00:12:59,490 --> 00:13:00,210
I'll wait for you.

214
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:28,020
[Please end my lease for me. Thanks. Jiang Ming]

215
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,440
[The Story Untold]

216
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,940
[Based on Twentine's novel "The Story Untold" on jjwxc.net]

217
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:16,060
[Episode 1]

218
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:21,660
[Three years ago]

219
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:28,540
[Nanhu, 2011]

220
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:18,750
[Jinxian Children's Home]

221
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:19,890
Nobody plays with him.

222
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:22,850
Give him something warm.

223
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,220
Yes.

224
00:16:25,390 --> 00:16:25,850
Ma'am.

225
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,610
I think someone's here to see you.

226
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:28,890
Over there.

227
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:35,650
[Jinxian Children's Home, 1987]
This was the year

228
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,380
your adoptive parents came to take you home.

229
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:38,970
Yeah.

230
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,940
It's good to have you back.

231
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,210
Your adoptive parents took you to Qingcheng.

232
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,950
You saw the world and learned a lot

233
00:16:49,950 --> 00:16:50,940
along the way.

234
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:52,940
In the end,

235
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,970
you always come home.

236
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:58,970
I want to open a studio here.

237
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,940
So how long will you be in Nanhu?

238
00:17:04,070 --> 00:17:04,820
I'm staying for good.

239
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:07,450
I'm on my own wherever I go anyway.

240
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:11,250
Zhao,

241
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,860
how have you been all these years?

242
00:17:18,230 --> 00:17:18,940
I've been fine.

243
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,850
When I got back,

244
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:25,290
I stopped by the site of the old children's home.

245
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:27,100
It's changed again.

246
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,450
It's a bar now.

247
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:29,900
I know.

248
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,770
They've made a real mess of the place.

249
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:33,690
I rented the place.

250
00:17:35,270 --> 00:17:36,420
What for?

251
00:17:37,710 --> 00:17:38,940
To open my studio.

252
00:18:11,230 --> 00:18:12,100
Anybody here?

253
00:18:13,750 --> 00:18:15,340
Hello? Is anybody here?

254
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:16,860
Coming!

255
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:21,530
Are you the one looking to rent this place?

256
00:18:21,790 --> 00:18:22,690
Yes, that's me.

257
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,680
I've been waiting for you for a while.

258
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:29,690
Come on in.

259
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:32,250
Look.

260
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:34,530
Beautiful view, isn't it?

261
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,180
And here's the inside.

262
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:40,940
The first floor is for business.

263
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,440
The second floor has private rooms.

264
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:46,860
You could live up there too.

265
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:49,940
Take a look.

266
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,580
Isn't the view beautiful?

267
00:18:54,310 --> 00:18:57,580
All the tables and chairs in here

268
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,620
are yours for free.

269
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,970
And you can get all the bottles in this cabinet

270
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:02,580
for a good price too.

271
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:05,210
You're getting a great deal here.

272
00:19:07,030 --> 00:19:07,730
Careful.

273
00:19:08,030 --> 00:19:09,180
It's a stray I've been looking after.

274
00:19:09,470 --> 00:19:10,420
I've fed it for three years,

275
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,420
and it still won't let me pet it.

276
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:13,180
It can't be tamed.

277
00:19:14,070 --> 00:19:15,420
It never asked you to look after it.

278
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:17,820
Sir,

279
00:19:18,230 --> 00:19:19,940
please put this couch by the...

280
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,010
There's a little door upstairs.

281
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:22,580
Go through it and put the couch against the wall.

282
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,250
Put this one

283
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,250
on the second floor, please.

284
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:25,730
You got it.

285
00:19:25,750 --> 00:19:26,730
Careful with that one, please.

286
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:27,860
It's fragile.

287
00:19:28,030 --> 00:19:28,450
All right.

288
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:28,970
Thanks.

289
00:19:56,220 --> 00:20:01,460
[Mangguang Border Inspection Station]

290
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:04,820
Stop.

291
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,010
Your papers.

292
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:14,970
Go ahead.

293
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:22,770
Buy one, please.

294
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:47,580
Move along.

295
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:48,420
Buy one, please.

296
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,140
Buy one, please.

297
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:01,900
Buy one, please.

298
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:09,940
Stop!

299
00:21:12,370 --> 00:21:13,410
What are you hauling?

300
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:14,970
Red wine.

301
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:26,440
This is all red wine?

302
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:28,010
Yes.

303
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:30,100
Let me see the test reports.

304
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,050
They're all here, Officer.

305
00:21:51,990 --> 00:21:53,380
It's just a few barrels of wine.

306
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,250
Is all this really necessary?

307
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,100
Lately, people have been mixing drugs into wine

308
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,180
to sneak them across the border.

309
00:21:58,210 --> 00:21:59,140
We're just being thorough.

310
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:00,100
Sounds like a waste of time.

311
00:22:00,770 --> 00:22:03,340
This wine's bound for Yunshan?

312
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:04,830
Yeah.

313
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:06,900
With freight costs this high,

314
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,730
the deal hardly seems worth it.

315
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:12,340
Papers, please.

316
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:21,530
Take off your sunglasses.

317
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,730
I think this wine goes for a lot these days.

318
00:22:27,710 --> 00:22:29,340
Besides, I'm just the delivery guy.

319
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:38,100
Tell him to open the trunk.

320
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,180
Open the trunk.

321
00:22:40,990 --> 00:22:41,420
I popped it.

322
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,900
Open those two barrels in the back

323
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,210
and check them too.

324
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:49,100
It won't open.

325
00:22:49,930 --> 00:22:50,770
I already popped it.

326
00:22:50,990 --> 00:22:51,530
Try it again.

327
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:53,730
You've already opened one barrel.

328
00:22:53,770 --> 00:22:55,620
If you open them all, I'll have to cover the loss.

329
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:56,250
Don't worry.

330
00:22:56,270 --> 00:22:57,860
It's a routine inspection.

331
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,660
We'll give you something in writing afterward.

332
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,180
Step back.

333
00:23:00,470 --> 00:23:01,140
No...

334
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:01,900
Wait, Officer.

335
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:02,580
Please cooperate.

336
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:03,250
No, wait.

337
00:23:04,510 --> 00:23:05,580
It won't open. Hurry up.

338
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:06,340
Open it.

339
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,140
It still won't open?

340
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:08,530
Get out.

341
00:23:08,550 --> 00:23:09,530
No, wait, Officer.

342
00:23:09,550 --> 00:23:10,580
No, Officer!

343
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:17,660
Is it jammed?

344
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,010
It's open.

345
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:27,380
I don't make that kind of money

346
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:28,770
on a single delivery!

347
00:23:34,360 --> 00:23:35,180
Stop interfering with the inspection!

348
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:35,860
Please cooperate.

349
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:36,660
No, Officer.

350
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:37,340
Let us do our job.

351
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:37,860
No...

352
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:38,820
Your papers, please.

353
00:23:41,470 --> 00:23:41,940
Freeze!

354
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:43,970
Hands up!

355
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:44,770
Now!

356
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:49,580
Take him away.

357
00:23:52,030 --> 00:23:53,730
Come here and check this!

358
00:23:58,750 --> 00:23:59,530
Jiang Ming.

359
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:01,050
What's with that wine?

360
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,250
So much sediment. What did you mix into it?

361
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,490
As red wine blends age,

362
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:08,900
they naturally develop

363
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:10,770
some sediment and oils.

364
00:24:10,790 --> 00:24:12,490
It's perfectly normal.

365
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,730
Anyone who drinks red wine knows that.

366
00:24:18,070 --> 00:24:18,940
Were the bottles refilled?

367
00:24:20,230 --> 00:24:21,580
The wine is 20 years old.

368
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:23,180
Of course the corks are damaged after soaking that long.

369
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:27,250
All right, then.

370
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:30,490
Take the whole case out and run lab tests

371
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:31,570
on every bottle.

372
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:32,340
Understood.

373
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:34,530
These are very expensive.

374
00:24:34,960 --> 00:24:36,080
Please cooperate.

375
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:54,730
Captain, the whole case came back clean.

376
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:04,690
You can go.

377
00:25:06,550 --> 00:25:07,210
Sorry for the trouble.

378
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:10,490
Lately, people have been mixing contraband into red wine

379
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:11,450
to sneak it across the border,

380
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:12,690
so we're checking more closely.

381
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:13,940
I hope you understand.

382
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:16,580
I understand.

383
00:25:18,070 --> 00:25:21,100
I just can't deliver the wine with the bottles open.

384
00:25:22,550 --> 00:25:23,140
So,

385
00:25:23,510 --> 00:25:24,250
should we pay for it?

386
00:25:24,710 --> 00:25:25,250
No need.

387
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:26,820
Officers,

388
00:25:27,550 --> 00:25:28,450
this really is good wine.

389
00:25:28,470 --> 00:25:29,380
Dry red wine from Margaux.

390
00:25:30,030 --> 00:25:31,180
Go ahead and enjoy it.

391
00:25:46,990 --> 00:25:48,800
Ming, are you in the clear?

392
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:50,690
Where's the shipment?

393
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:53,050
Five kilos of No. 4 heroin.

394
00:25:53,100 --> 00:25:54,250
All delivered safely.

395
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:04,180
That was close at the checkpoint today.

396
00:26:04,990 --> 00:26:06,180
Good thing you were there, Ming.

397
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:08,100
If they'd opened the barrels and tested them,

398
00:26:08,790 --> 00:26:09,620
I'd have been busted.

399
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:12,140
Your mix is a little too dense.

400
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,660
That'll make it harder to purify.

401
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:16,340
Tell that guy to work fast.

402
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:17,770
It's a really good batch.

403
00:26:19,070 --> 00:26:20,250
Okay, got it.

404
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:22,340
By the way, Ming,

405
00:26:24,270 --> 00:26:26,050
how did you doctor the wine in your van?

406
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:27,940
How come it passed even the lab tests?

407
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,140
It was real wine.

408
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:31,970
Real wine?

409
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:36,340
Then why did the densimeter go off?

410
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:39,860
Even real wine

411
00:26:40,510 --> 00:26:41,490
produces volatile compounds

412
00:26:41,750 --> 00:26:42,900
as it ages,

413
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:45,210
no matter how well it's sealed.

414
00:26:46,310 --> 00:26:46,970
Get it?

415
00:26:48,750 --> 00:26:49,860
Should've paid attention in school.

416
00:26:51,750 --> 00:26:52,530
Get that for me.

417
00:26:58,470 --> 00:26:59,420
Ming's driving.

418
00:27:02,470 --> 00:27:03,080
Okay, got it.

419
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:05,340
Mr. Bai asked

420
00:27:05,840 --> 00:27:06,970
when we could recover the shipment

421
00:27:06,990 --> 00:27:08,290
Liu Wei left at the bar.

422
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:09,580
Some woman just moved in

423
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,450
and took over the place.

424
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:11,140
How can we find it now?

425
00:27:14,270 --> 00:27:14,940
Don't worry.

426
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,730
Let's go take a look first.

427
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:23,770
There you are.

428
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:26,860
I brought you a treat.

429
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:32,250
Go on and eat.

430
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:35,140
You won't even eat this?

431
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:37,940
Picky, aren't you?

432
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:11,450
Don't move!

433
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:27,530
Hey, beautiful.

434
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:29,100
What are you doing?

435
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:30,860
I'm no thief.

436
00:28:31,270 --> 00:28:32,420
How did you get in?

437
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:41,100
I let myself in. Nothing shady about it.

438
00:28:43,230 --> 00:28:44,100
Is Curly around?

439
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:46,490
No.

440
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,900
I rented the place from him.

441
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,620
He left Nanhu a while ago.

442
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,580
What do you need?

443
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:56,970
I left a few things here.

444
00:28:57,790 --> 00:28:59,100
I'll go as soon as I find them.

445
00:29:03,030 --> 00:29:03,940
You can put that down.

446
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:04,770
Aren't your arms tired?

447
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:11,940
Did you work here?

448
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:21,530
A bartender?

449
00:29:29,990 --> 00:29:30,860
Then could you

450
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:32,900
mix this one for me?

451
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:36,420
Flame Sprite?

452
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:39,420
It's made with absinthe.

453
00:29:39,790 --> 00:29:40,450
What?

454
00:29:41,270 --> 00:29:42,050
Don't know how to make it?

455
00:30:23,070 --> 00:30:24,180
As far as I know,

456
00:30:24,710 --> 00:30:26,900
absinthe is supposed to be

457
00:30:27,230 --> 00:30:28,290
clear, right?

458
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:31,180
It's what drove Vincent van Gogh mad.

459
00:30:34,070 --> 00:30:36,960
Metelka. It's Czech.

460
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:40,820
This one's been infused with herbs,

461
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:42,820
so the thujone's gone.

462
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:45,940
You'd only hallucinate if you had too much thujone.

463
00:30:47,790 --> 00:30:48,450
Try it.

464
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:53,140
You try it.

465
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,050
How is it?

466
00:31:11,070 --> 00:31:11,580
It's fake.

467
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:28,420
I read online

468
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,970
that this place went out of business

469
00:31:30,510 --> 00:31:31,730
because the drinks were terrible.

470
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:33,900
Sounds about right.

471
00:31:37,510 --> 00:31:38,860
By the way, what did you

472
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:39,620
come back for?

473
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:40,290
I'll help you find them.

474
00:31:41,710 --> 00:31:42,250
Get over here!

475
00:31:42,270 --> 00:31:42,940
Stop hitting me!

476
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:45,580
Ming,

477
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:46,690
I found Curly.

478
00:31:49,070 --> 00:31:49,620
Ming,

479
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:51,100
I messed up.

480
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:53,050
Please let me off this once.

481
00:32:08,840 --> 00:32:09,580
Let's talk.

482
00:32:10,270 --> 00:32:12,290
I'll refund your rent in full.

483
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:14,180
Give me back the bar.

484
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,340
Walk away from the lease.

485
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:19,860
Name your price.

486
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,450
That's a little low, isn't it?

487
00:32:32,550 --> 00:32:33,970
I signed the contract with him.

488
00:32:34,270 --> 00:32:35,210
It's all in writing.

489
00:32:35,510 --> 00:32:36,250
That's what I'm going by.

490
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:39,690
I'll say it again.

491
00:32:40,070 --> 00:32:42,050
This bar is ours.

492
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:43,490
The bar's yours?

493
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:46,180
Why should I believe you?

494
00:32:52,790 --> 00:32:54,250
Even if that's true,

495
00:32:54,510 --> 00:32:56,010
that's between you and him.

496
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:58,250
Now please leave.

497
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:00,380
Ming, no point reasoning with her.

498
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:02,340
Whether you agree or not,

499
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:04,100
we're taking this bar back today.

500
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:08,140
You're right. There's no point reasoning with thugs.

501
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:09,380
Who are you calling a thug?

502
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,860
One of you is all talk.

503
00:33:11,710 --> 00:33:12,970
The other lies through his teeth.

504
00:33:12,990 --> 00:33:14,580
I think you crooks are ripping each other off.

505
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:16,620
If you refuse to leave,

506
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,820
I'll have to call the police.

507
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:26,490
Scared now?

508
00:33:27,310 --> 00:33:28,580
Weren't you looking for something?

509
00:33:29,070 --> 00:33:30,900
Why don't we have the police come look for it?

510
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:33,730
Jianshan.

511
00:33:48,270 --> 00:33:49,140
Sorry for the trouble.

512
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:53,690
Let's go.

513
00:33:56,750 --> 00:33:57,290
Ming.

514
00:33:59,710 --> 00:34:00,180
Come here.

515
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:01,580
Wait...

516
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:02,340
Man, I...

517
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:02,940
Just hear me out!

518
00:34:23,550 --> 00:34:24,170
Ming.

519
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:25,220
Ming, I messed up.

520
00:34:25,240 --> 00:34:26,010
I messed up.

521
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:26,900
Please let me go.

522
00:34:27,240 --> 00:34:27,900
Where's the shipment?

523
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,300
Shipment? What shipment?

524
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:32,970
Still playing dumb?

525
00:34:35,590 --> 00:34:37,130
The No. 4 from Zhalan.

526
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,050
Curly,

527
00:34:39,470 --> 00:34:40,490
if you still won't talk,

528
00:34:41,150 --> 00:34:42,650
I'll hand you over to your boss, Liu Wei.

529
00:34:43,070 --> 00:34:43,700
No, please don't.

530
00:34:44,720 --> 00:34:45,820
If my boss finds out,

531
00:34:45,840 --> 00:34:46,940
he'll kill me.

532
00:34:47,990 --> 00:34:48,420
Ming,

533
00:34:48,990 --> 00:34:50,530
I really don't know about any shipment.

534
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:52,860
Liu Wei only asked me to look after the bar.

535
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:54,900
I really don't know anything else.

536
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:57,220
I don't get mixed up in anything else.

537
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,780
What's the deal with that woman in the bar?

538
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,610
I don't know her.

539
00:35:04,190 --> 00:35:06,170
She saw the rental listing online

540
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:07,490
and came to me.

541
00:35:08,630 --> 00:35:09,820
I... I swear

542
00:35:10,280 --> 00:35:11,130
it's true.

543
00:35:11,190 --> 00:35:12,220
I needed money,

544
00:35:12,220 --> 00:35:13,200
so I rented the place to her.

545
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:14,240
I'll give you all the money.

546
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:15,170
Go.

547
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:21,280
Thanks, Ming. Thank you.

548
00:35:23,840 --> 00:35:24,300
Ming,

549
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:25,970
you're just letting him go?

550
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:30,900
What if that punk already took the shipment?

551
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:32,740
He wouldn't dare.

552
00:35:51,840 --> 00:35:52,490
Boss,

553
00:35:53,190 --> 00:35:54,790
we couldn't find Curly. He took off.

554
00:35:56,880 --> 00:35:58,860
So Jiang Ming's the one

555
00:36:00,550 --> 00:36:02,130
who went to the bar?

556
00:36:03,470 --> 00:36:03,900
Yeah.

557
00:36:04,550 --> 00:36:05,570
Mr. Bai's orders.

558
00:36:12,960 --> 00:36:16,010
Instead of letting me run my own warehouse,

559
00:36:16,030 --> 00:36:17,170
he's putting Jiang Ming in charge.

560
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:19,820
Mr. Bai's never thought much of me.

561
00:36:21,630 --> 00:36:22,970
Jiang Ming thinks even less of me.

562
00:36:26,070 --> 00:36:26,940
They keep telling me

563
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:27,740
to wait.

564
00:36:31,630 --> 00:36:34,010
How can you all be so useless?

565
00:36:34,030 --> 00:36:36,220
Now I've got to hand over my own warehouse to him!

566
00:36:42,630 --> 00:36:43,300
Boss,

567
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:44,820
I've been thinking.

568
00:36:45,070 --> 00:36:46,940
We hid that shipment pretty well.

569
00:36:47,670 --> 00:36:49,030
Jiang Ming might not find it.

570
00:36:50,110 --> 00:36:51,150
We can beat him to it

571
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:52,870
and get the shipment back.

572
00:36:56,110 --> 00:36:58,800
Fine. You get the bar.

573
00:36:59,510 --> 00:37:01,340
I get the shipment.

574
00:37:04,510 --> 00:37:06,490
Just you wait.

575
00:37:07,510 --> 00:37:10,010
I'll show you what I'm capable of.

576
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:14,050
How's that?

577
00:37:14,760 --> 00:37:15,530
Looks good.

578
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,130
Come on, let's carry it out.

579
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:23,740
Okay.

580
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:45,300
[Jinxian Pottery Studio]
Ming, the new sign's already up.

581
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:46,940
You can add a little more water.

582
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:50,170
Be polite when we go in.

583
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:51,260
Okay.

584
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:00,260
I'm sorry.

585
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:00,970
It's okay.

586
00:38:01,550 --> 00:38:02,170
Be good.

587
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:03,860
Don't do that again, okay?

588
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:04,700
You two again?

589
00:38:05,590 --> 00:38:06,490
It's only been a few days,

590
00:38:07,110 --> 00:38:08,380
and you've already opened a youth center?

591
00:38:10,990 --> 00:38:11,780
Here to sign up?

592
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:14,300
"Anyone under 22 or enrolled in school

593
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,570
gets three free trial sessions

594
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:18,820
and a free pack of clay to practice with."

595
00:38:20,760 --> 00:38:21,380
How do I sign up?

596
00:38:22,550 --> 00:38:23,300
Which one of you

597
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:25,260
is under 22?

598
00:38:27,110 --> 00:38:27,740
Me.

599
00:38:29,070 --> 00:38:30,260
Then please show me your ID

600
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:31,050
so I can sign you up.

601
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:35,860
Do you have to take this so seriously?

602
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:37,700
If you two aren't signing up,

603
00:38:37,990 --> 00:38:39,050
I'll get back to work.

604
00:38:39,070 --> 00:38:40,570
I'm busy today. Excuse me.

605
00:38:41,990 --> 00:38:42,570
By the way,

606
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:44,940
getting a fake ID is illegal too.

607
00:38:45,440 --> 00:38:46,050
Ms. Yang.

608
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:51,820
Since you're so busy,

609
00:38:52,470 --> 00:38:53,740
I'll get right to the point.

610
00:38:54,240 --> 00:38:56,340
Have you thought about what we discussed last time?

611
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:57,820
There's nothing to think about.

612
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:00,050
You can keep pushing,

613
00:39:00,150 --> 00:39:01,530
but I've got a signed contract.

614
00:39:01,550 --> 00:39:02,860
We can take this straight to court.

615
00:39:03,510 --> 00:39:04,220
No need to go that far.

616
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:07,570
I've got something I need to keep here.

617
00:39:08,670 --> 00:39:10,220
If you turn the place over to me,

618
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:11,260
everything else

619
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:12,570
is negotiable.

620
00:39:13,070 --> 00:39:14,860
We tore out everything that had to go

621
00:39:14,880 --> 00:39:16,090
and redid whatever needed changing.

622
00:39:16,110 --> 00:39:18,900
I didn't see anything valuable.

623
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:20,780
Can I go in and take a look?

624
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:21,780
Sorry, no.

625
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:23,130
Class is in session.

626
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:29,570
Oh.

627
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:31,090
I just remembered.

628
00:39:31,840 --> 00:39:34,860
We took the last load of trash out this morning.

629
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:35,820
I didn't look too closely.

630
00:39:36,320 --> 00:39:37,490
It's right there by the corner.

631
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:40,420
If your stuff's here at all,

632
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:42,260
try digging through that pile of trash.

633
00:39:45,360 --> 00:39:46,260
Trash, huh?

634
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:50,780
Are we really going to dig through it?

635
00:39:53,670 --> 00:39:54,940
If you hadn't held me back,

636
00:39:55,460 --> 00:39:56,380
I would've gotten tough with her,

637
00:39:56,840 --> 00:39:57,780
and she'd have caved for sure.

638
00:39:59,240 --> 00:40:00,610
She opened this place to the public

639
00:40:00,620 --> 00:40:02,570
[Jinxian Pottery Studio]
just to tie our hands.

640
00:40:03,670 --> 00:40:05,820
The more attention she draws, the less we can do.

641
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:10,380
Is she here by herself?

642
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:12,860
Seems like it.

643
00:40:13,400 --> 00:40:14,700
I think she's from out of town.

644
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:16,890
Want me to look into her connections?

645
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:17,900
No need.

646
00:40:23,800 --> 00:40:25,420
Getting in won't be easy now.

647
00:40:25,420 --> 00:40:26,420
[Jinxian Pottery Studio]

648
00:40:26,460 --> 00:40:29,620
[Hands-On Lessons with Experienced Potters, Tuesday to Sunday]

649
00:40:33,590 --> 00:40:34,130
Ms. Yang,

650
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,450
someone came by

651
00:40:35,470 --> 00:40:36,700
to ask about the classes.

652
00:40:36,880 --> 00:40:38,170
He's waiting outside.

653
00:40:38,190 --> 00:40:39,650
Okay, I'll go see him now.

654
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:40,340
Okay.

655
00:41:16,550 --> 00:41:17,010
It's you?

656
00:41:43,500 --> 00:41:45,980
♪Rain♪

657
00:41:46,180 --> 00:41:48,980
♪Falls on a sea of faces♪

658
00:41:51,140 --> 00:41:53,380
♪You♪

659
00:41:54,060 --> 00:41:57,100
♪Walk toward me, silhouetted against the light♪

660
00:41:58,620 --> 00:42:02,060
♪After countless days and nights of waiting♪

661
00:42:02,180 --> 00:42:04,340
♪My heart beats out♪

662
00:42:04,500 --> 00:42:06,660
♪A wild rhythm♪

663
00:42:06,860 --> 00:42:08,380
♪Here we are together again♪

664
00:42:08,660 --> 00:42:11,860
♪You came back for me♪

665
00:42:14,820 --> 00:42:16,540
♪Say it♪

666
00:42:17,580 --> 00:42:20,060
♪With a wordless confession of love♪

667
00:42:22,300 --> 00:42:23,740
♪Tears♪

668
00:42:25,140 --> 00:42:27,940
♪Burn against my chest♪

669
00:42:29,900 --> 00:42:33,540
♪I've never forgotten what you said♪

670
00:42:33,620 --> 00:42:35,500
♪Day after day♪

671
00:42:35,700 --> 00:42:37,220
♪I replayed the past♪

672
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:39,580
♪Waiting till you♪

673
00:42:39,780 --> 00:42:44,180
♪Were back by my side♪

674
00:42:44,260 --> 00:42:47,860
♪After all the time we lost♪

675
00:42:48,180 --> 00:42:51,860
♪This moment finally makes us whole♪

676
00:42:52,100 --> 00:42:55,100
♪We hold each other through tears♪

677
00:42:55,460 --> 00:42:59,540
♪We promise never to let this change again♪

678
00:43:00,300 --> 00:43:04,020
♪At last you're here♪

679
00:43:04,380 --> 00:43:07,660
♪At last our paths come together♪

680
00:43:08,100 --> 00:43:11,220
♪At last there are no regrets♪

681
00:43:11,460 --> 00:43:16,460
♪You promised you'd come back♪

682
00:43:17,140 --> 00:43:19,260
♪We sing a song of reunion♪

683
00:43:19,460 --> 00:43:21,460
♪Time stands still♪

684
00:43:21,780 --> 00:43:25,060
♪Right here in this moment♪

685
00:43:25,580 --> 00:43:27,900
♪You say it was♪

686
00:43:28,500 --> 00:43:33,060
♪Worth it♪

687
00:43:35,220 --> 00:43:38,540
♪At last you're here♪

688
00:43:39,180 --> 00:43:42,740
♪At last our paths come together♪

689
00:43:43,060 --> 00:43:46,180
♪At last there are no regrets♪

690
